        <detaileddescription>
<para>The default implementation checks populates the <computeroutput>SavedRegs</computeroutput> bitset with all registers which are modified in the function, targets may override this function to save additional registers. This method also sets up the register scavenger ensuring there is a free register or a frameindex available. This method should not be called by any passes outside of PEI, because it may change state passed in by <computeroutput>MF</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>RS</computeroutput>. The preferred interface outside PEI is getCalleeSaves. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
